<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Monotonicity score, defined as the Pearson correlation between <math id="A1.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,2,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,2,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the test scores <math id="A1.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{score_{0},score_{50},score_{100},\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>50</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>100</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{score_{0},score_{50},score_{100},\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math> recorded every 50 steps. Our method exhibits the highest monotonicity score overall, indicating it promotes steady improvement between training steps.</figcaption>
</figure>
